==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{af|ru|пере-|носи́ть}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|переноси́ть}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-переносить.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|переноси́ть|impf|pf=перенести́}}

# to [[transfer]], to [[carry]], to [[transport]] {{q|somewhere}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[он|Он]] [[в]] мы́сли '''перено́сит''' [[себя́]] [[в]] соверше́нно [[друго́й]] [[мир]]|He '''transfers''' himself mentally to a completely different world}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[она|Она́]] '''переноси́ла''' лёгкое [[те́ло]] [[через]] [[поро́г]]|She '''carried''' the lightweight body through the sill}}
# to [[carry over]] (a [[word]]) to the [[next]] [[line]]
# to [[postpone]], to [[put off]]
# to [[extend]] {{q|to}}
# to [[bear]], to [[endure]], to [[stand]], to [[tolerate]]
#: {{uxi|ru|'''переноси́ть''' [[весьма́]] [[сто́йко]]|To endure very persistently}}

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|impf|4c|переноси́ть|prpp=+}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|переноси́ть|pf|impf=перена́шивать}}

# to [[carry]] ([[all]] or [[many]] things) from one [[place]] to [[another]]
# to [[wear]] ([[all]] or [[many]] [[item]]s of [[clothing]])
# to [[carry]] (a [[child]]) [[too]] [[long]] in a [[pregnancy]]

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|pf|4c+p|переноси́ть}}

